in the Fire Festival.

256
00:17:28,820 --> 00:17:31,173
But now we can at least buy fresh water.

257
00:17:31,500 --> 00:17:35,265
We burned down the bandits' hideout
because they stole our food.

258
00:17:35,440 --> 00:17:38,337
I thought they'd come seeking
revenge and we'd wipe them out.

259
00:17:38,420 --> 00:17:42,000
But instead, they keep stealing
more food than ever before!

260
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:48,497
I'm thinking you might have
something to do with all this.

261
00:17:48,580 --> 00:17:50,180
We don't know anything!

262
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:54,071
I heard an army of samurai are
planning to make a big raid.

263
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:56,437
Do you think that's why
they're stealing food?

264
00:17:56,520 --> 00:17:58,991
I don't know, but don't let him hear that!

265
00:18:00,320 --> 00:18:01,150
Hey!

266
00:18:01,233 --> 00:18:02,506
What are you muttering about?

267
00:18:03,860 --> 00:18:06,000
Please, allow me! I'll show you!

268
00:18:06,260 --> 00:18:09,260
There's no need for any of
these people to be hurt.

269
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:10,710
Hotsuru!

270
00:18:11,260 --> 00:18:12,120
Show me?

271
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:16,417
So you're saying you know
what happened to the food?

272
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:18,177
You'll see once we get there.

273
00:18:18,260 --> 00:18:19,680
It's a bit far, though.

274
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:30,080
If you need that much food, you
must have recruited many allies.

275
00:18:30,660 --> 00:18:32,660
You're here, aren't you, Keen?

276
00:18:33,220 --> 00:18:35,338
You've returned to the land of Wano!

277
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:38,820
I was stunned when I saw Kikunojo.

278
00:18:41,940 --> 00:18:43,220
Don't worry, Keen.

279
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:44,977
You can rely on me.

280
00:18:45,060 --> 00:18:47,580
I will draw the attention of our enemies.

281
00:18:47,860 --> 00:18:49,320
Your secret is safe.

282
00:18:49,640 --> 00:18:51,480
I won't let them find you

283
00:18:52,560 --> 00:18:54,020
Save this country!

284
00:18:54,460 --> 00:18:57,120
Bring back the glory of the Kozuki clan!

285
00:18:58,820 --> 00:19:00,000
Otsuru, stop this!

286
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:02,024
You don't have to cover for us!

287
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:03,720
It's all right now.

288
00:19:03,960 --> 00:19:07,431
All we wanted was to eat our
fill even once before we died!

289
00:19:09,820 --> 00:19:12,540
Does that mean you bastards did it?

290
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:21,240
Ah, Koza!

291
00:19:22,740 --> 00:19:25,940
You can all say hello
to your lord in hell!

292
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:30,580
Did you find the ship? Yes, sir!

293
00:19:31,120 --> 00:19:32,680
It's in sight right now!

294
00:19:33,840 --> 00:19:36,117
Sure you want us to let
loose on this thing?

295
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:38,500
I told you to do it, so do it already!

296
00:19:42,040 --> 00:19:43,040
Burn it!

297
00:19:43,820 --> 00:19:44,650
Roger!

298
00:20:00,280 --> 00:20:01,400
Missing, complete!

299
00:20:05,360 --> 00:20:08,007
You really thought I'd
let you have your way?

300
00:20:08,300 --> 00:20:09,960
I am the Shogun!

301
00:20:10,620 --> 00:20:11,800
No, the bridges!

302
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:17,217
The great bridge between Koby
and Udon has been destroyed.

303
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:19,060
Don't stop there!

304
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:23,957
The great bridge between Koby
and Udon has been destroyed.

305
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:26,140
This is what you get?

306
00:20:27,740 --> 00:20:29,093
What the hell happened?

307
00:20:29,260 --> 00:20:30,677
Someone just blew up the bridge.

308
00:20:30,760 --> 00:20:32,437
We can't get to the other side.

309
00:20:32,520 --> 00:20:33,477
Something's wrong.

310
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:35,557
The enemy must have discovered our plan.

311
00:20:35,640 --> 00:20:38,300
All that remains is the port.

312
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:43,397
We destroyed every ship in
the port as you ordered, sir.

313
00:20:43,480 --> 00:20:44,397
Excellent.

314
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:46,037
We'll rebuild everything.

315
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:48,297
Once this is over, unfortunately,

316
00:20:48,380 --> 00:20:51,317
I've yet to see the Akasaya
samurai or any of the

317
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:54,337
troops they've recruited but
I know they're out there.

318
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:58,557
The tale of the samurai
who traveled through

319
00:20:58,640 --> 00:21:01,957
time from 20 years in the past of course,

320
00:21:02,040 --> 00:21:07,040
no one believed that story but perhaps
they will when I show them one?

321
00:21:08,620 --> 00:21:09,450
their heads.

322
00:21:09,533 --> 00:21:13,837
No, even if I did show them,
it's too strange to believe.

323
00:21:13,920 --> 00:21:15,740
Yasui knew exactly what he was

324
00:21:18,220 --> 00:21:19,050
doing.

325
00:21:19,133 --> 00:21:20,957
He made it sound even more ridiculous.

326
00:21:21,040 --> 00:21:23,597
But my information is credible.

327
00:21:23,680 --> 00:21:24,720
The Akasaya

328
00:21:26,880 --> 00:21:29,277
members are indeed alive.

329
00:21:29,360 --> 00:21:33,478
I don't care if everyone in this
blasted country thinks I've gone mad.

330
00:21:33,700 --> 00:21:36,641
I have the authority to
do as I please either way.

331
00:21:37,760 --> 00:21:42,720
Not only did I destroy their ships,
I've blocked every last route to Cage?

332
00:21:43,280 --> 00:21:44,110
Port.

333
00:21:44,193 --> 00:21:45,280
4,000 troops.

334
00:21:45,700 --> 00:21:47,440
You did a splendid job.

335
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:51,565
But not a single one of them is
making it to that port tomorrow.

336
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:55,580
You won't even get a chance
to exact your revenge.

337
00:21:58,340 --> 00:22:01,420
I'll kill you again, Ghost of Akazaya!

338
00:22:01,940 --> 00:22:02,770
Ha!

339
00:22:02,853 --> 00:22:03,797
Follow in despair!

340
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:06,720
See how truly helpless you are!

341
00:22:14,740 --> 00:22:16,160
Stop the sadness!

342
00:22:16,540 --> 00:22:18,011
You can't take that boat!

343
00:22:18,140 --> 00:22:19,800
All of you will die insane!

344
00:22:20,880 --> 00:22:23,320
We should turn back! We can regroup!

345
00:22:23,760 --> 00:22:25,477
Let's wait for another chance!

346
00:22:25,560 --> 00:22:28,120
We cannot throw away this opportunity.

347
00:22:28,580 --> 00:22:31,874
The chance you speak of will
not occur for another year.

348
00:22:32,820 --> 00:22:35,897
Soon they will discover that
we've taken control of Udon.

349
00:22:35,980 --> 00:22:38,037
There will be nowhere left for us to hide.

350
00:22:38,120 --> 00:22:39,000
Not anymore.

351
00:22:40,540 --> 00:22:42,597
Kaido will use the full
strength of his army

352
00:22:42,680 --> 00:22:45,327
to hunt down every last
rebel in the country.

353
00:22:46,980 --> 00:22:49,160
We can't keep stealing their food.

354
00:22:49,340 --> 00:22:51,046
They'll catch on soon enough.

355
00:22:51,200 --> 00:22:54,780
You heard what happened before
we departed from Kuri, right?

356
00:22:55,900 --> 00:23:01,120
The people of Okobore Town believed in
us and took the blame for our crimes.

357
00:23:01,780 --> 00:23:03,400
They were burned alive.

358
00:23:04,100 --> 00:23:07,280
Among them was my wife.

359
00:23:11,020 --> 00:23:12,600
Please allow us to go.

360
00:23:15,760 --> 00:23:17,080
I will not.

361
00:23:17,300 --> 00:23:18,540
You want us to flee?

362
00:23:18,820 --> 00:23:19,820
Live in disgrace?

363
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:22,259
You would deny us even our dignity?

364
00:23:23,620 --> 00:23:25,720
But what will become of me?

365
00:23:26,260 --> 00:23:30,420
We want you to live, of
course, alongside Lady Yuri.

366
00:23:30,660 --> 00:23:33,131
You're saying that you want to abandon me?

367
00:23:34,180 --> 00:23:37,720
Your father began without a
single supporter to his name.

368
00:23:37,980 --> 00:23:41,860
We were lucky, and we are grateful
that we were able to meet him.

369
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:46,717
He took a bunch of fools and turned them
into samurai because he believed in us.

370
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:50,160
So we are here as retainers to our Lord,

371
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:55,140
and I shall proudly fight in his
name, to the bitter end, if need be.

372
00:23:58,740 --> 00:23:59,570
Don't go!

373
00:23:59,653 --> 00:24:01,977
You can't leave me, Kin'emon! Please!

374
00:24:02,060 --> 00:24:04,980
I can't stand to lose anyone else!

375
00:24:09,040 --> 00:24:10,600
Listen up, all of you.

376
00:24:10,900 --> 00:24:13,397
This country has been
isolated for centuries.

377
00:24:13,480 --> 00:24:18,160
As its stewards, it is a decision
deeply tied to the Kozuki clan.

378
00:24:18,640 --> 00:24:20,420
But the times are changing.

379
00:24:20,860 --> 00:24:23,120
This world will soon enter a new era.

380
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:28,580
Before this comes to pass, our land
of Wano must be prepared to meet it!

381
00:24:28,780 --> 00:24:30,800
We must open our borders!

382
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:58,200
The tale of Odin begins 41
years ago in the Flower Capital.

383
00:24:59,900 --> 00:25:02,180
Kozuki Odin has returned!

384
00:25:02,880 --> 00:25:05,704
Hide your wives quickly,
and your daughters too!

385
00:25:06,560 --> 00:25:09,207
Hide the livestock quick,
hide the livestock!

386
00:25:11,560 --> 00:25:14,277
Looks like his latest escape
plan must have failed.

387
00:25:14,360 --> 00:25:15,697
What is wrong with you?

388
00:25:15,780 --> 00:25:16,957
Don't you ever learn?

389
00:25:17,040 --> 00:25:22,860
The man was well known in the
capital but not always well liked.

390
00:25:34,120 --> 00:25:37,280
Damn it, I can't breathe!
